  "note": "Urban district election, 15 May 1936. There was no contest: the twelve seats were filled by nomination and the new council was printed in full (Northern Whig and Belfast Post, 8 May 1936, p. 8). Seven Nationalists and five Unionists, all returned unopposed. Messrs. J. Feenan and P. Ford were the only re-elected Nationalists; J. Gibson and J. Dixon were new Unionists, Gibson a former member. Returned unopposed."
